"""External-auditor engine for the yitc-v2 CLI — invocation/adapter, prompt building, verdict
parsing, the audit-loop ceiling helpers, and the audit-YAML I/O (CHARTER §P4a "external auditor").

This is the home for the auditor ENGINE that used to be scattered across bin/yitc-v2 (the L3700→16000
spread the SPEC-0080 §P-A4 navigation-cost lens flagged). bin/yitc-v2 keeps the argparse VERBS
(cmd_audit / cmd_audit_adhoc / cmd_audit_consult), the task-lifecycle gates, the plan-gate builders, and
the provider-dispatch identity layer (AUDIT_PROVIDERS + _invoke_auditor) — and a thin residue under the
historical names that delegates here, so every `yitc.<symbol>` test contract + the SPEC-0050 cmd_audit
content-hash stay byte-identical (T-9248).

Identity-agnostic KERNEL module (SPEC-0073 bin/ HARD class — travels with the engine). The
host-coupled inputs the engine must NOT read itself — REPO_ROOT, DECISIONS_DIR, AUDIT_CONFIG_PATH,
AUDIT_PASS_CEILING, the host helper callables (_die, the git/prompt-section helpers), and the
monkeypatchable provider-dispatch — are RESOLVED BY THE CALLER (the bin/yitc-v2 wrappers) and passed in
by INJECTION (the state.py `rel_root` / events.py `guard=` precedent), so a `-C` rebind and the test
attribute-replacement of `yitc.<symbol>` are honored by the host wrapper at call time. The concrete
codex binding (CHARTER §P4b) already lived in this code; it travels with the module. Behaviour is
byte-identical to the inline original — the test suite is the oracle.
"""
